1
00:00:09,774 --> 00:00:11,101
It looks like a gift.

2
00:00:11,901 --> 00:00:16,199
OpenAI says more than 1 billion people use it every week.

3
00:00:16,199 --> 00:00:18,461
The vast majority pay nothing.

4
00:00:19,362 --> 00:00:22,228
So… what are you paying with?

5
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:32,802
November 30, 2022.

6
00:00:32,802 --> 00:00:34,950
ChatGPT launches.

7
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:35,582
Free.

8
00:00:35,832 --> 00:00:38,013
A million users in five days.

9
00:00:38,013 --> 00:00:40,194
Critics called it unreliable.

10
00:00:40,194 --> 00:00:41,548
Users kept coming.

11
00:00:41,798 --> 00:00:42,492
Why free?

12
00:00:42,492 --> 00:00:46,733
OpenAI's launch post said it: “to get users’ feedback.”

13
00:00:46,983 --> 00:00:48,742
And the next model, GPT-4?

14
00:00:48,742 --> 00:00:49,825
Already trained.

15
00:00:49,825 --> 00:00:52,193
Three months before you said hello.

16
00:00:52,443 --> 00:00:54,126
Scale built the engine.

17
00:00:54,126 --> 00:00:55,150
Bigger models.

18
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:55,882
More data.

19
00:00:55,882 --> 00:00:56,833
More compute.

20
00:00:57,083 --> 00:00:59,946
Then OpenAI tuned it with human feedback.

21
00:00:59,946 --> 00:01:03,297
“Including feedback submitted by ChatGPT users.”

22
00:01:03,547 --> 00:01:05,647
The free product was shaping the next one.

23
00:01:07,547 --> 00:01:08,706
It has a name.

24
00:01:08,706 --> 00:01:10,195
The data flywheel.

25
00:01:10,395 --> 00:01:11,252
You use it.

26
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,403
Your feedback becomes signal.

27
00:01:16,902 --> 00:01:18,346
The model improves.

28
00:01:18,346 --> 00:01:19,639
More people come.

29
00:01:19,639 --> 00:01:21,387
The wheel spins faster.

30
00:01:21,637 --> 00:01:23,652
Even your thumbs-up counts.

31
00:01:23,652 --> 00:01:29,921
In 2025, a ChatGPT update added a reward signal from thumbs-up and thumbs-down data.

32
00:01:30,121 --> 00:01:34,466
It helped make the model so flattering that OpenAI rolled the update back.

33
00:01:34,716 --> 00:01:36,455
You're not just the customer.

34
00:01:36,455 --> 00:01:37,955
You're part of the wheel.

35
00:01:39,655 --> 00:01:41,809
Startups rushed to wrap the models.

36
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:44,797
Then ChatGPT learned to read PDFs.

37
00:01:44,997 --> 00:01:48,915
One reaction online: “Many startups just died today.”

38
00:01:49,065 --> 00:01:50,873
A reaction, not a verdict.

39
00:01:50,873 --> 00:01:52,751
Thin wrappers were exposed.

40
00:01:52,751 --> 00:01:55,602
Strong companies got squeezed, or bought.

41
00:01:55,852 --> 00:02:00,701
Sam Altman's warning: bet that the models won't improve, and you'll get steamrolled.

42
00:02:00,901 --> 00:02:02,395
Each model opens doors.

43
00:02:02,395 --> 00:02:04,474
The next release can close them.

44
00:02:06,174 --> 00:02:07,985
Then the wheel turned to the coders.

45
00:02:08,135 --> 00:02:09,455
The memos came.

46
00:02:09,455 --> 00:02:10,071
Use AI.

47
00:02:10,071 --> 00:02:12,888
Shopify: a baseline expectation.

48
00:02:12,888 --> 00:02:16,584
Microsoft, reportedly: no longer optional.

49
00:02:17,184 --> 00:02:22,382
In 2023, AI could fix about 2% of real GitHub issues on a benchmark.

50
00:02:22,532 --> 00:02:28,962
By February 2026, Anthropic reported about 80%, for Claude Opus 4.6.

51
00:02:29,162 --> 00:02:30,664
Then Claude Opus 5.5.

52
00:02:30,664 --> 00:02:35,742
Anthropic puts it at the level of its larger Fable model, on most work.

53
00:02:35,992 --> 00:02:38,086
And your code, on personal plans?

54
00:02:38,236 --> 00:02:42,686
GitHub believes the future of AI-assisted development depends on real-world

55
00:02:42,686 --> 00:02:43,695
interaction data.

56
00:02:43,695 --> 00:02:45,178
From developers like you.

57
00:02:47,078 --> 00:02:48,834
So why is it nearly free?

58
00:02:48,984 --> 00:02:50,708
Investor billions.

59
00:02:50,708 --> 00:02:52,335
A race for users.

60
00:02:52,335 --> 00:02:52,718
Ads.

61
00:02:52,718 --> 00:02:54,059
Falling costs.

62
00:02:54,259 --> 00:02:57,103
And part of the price is paid in data.

63
00:02:57,653 --> 00:02:58,445
Yours.

64
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:00,420
There's a switch.

65
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:02,887
But most people never touch their defaults.

66
00:03:03,087 --> 00:03:03,927
It's a trade.

67
00:03:03,927 --> 00:03:05,026
Often a good one.

68
00:03:05,026 --> 00:03:06,965
Just know what you're trading.

69
00:03:07,565 --> 00:03:09,710
So our app just calls the model—

70
00:03:09,710 --> 00:03:13,484
But if your plan is a thin wrapper on someone else's model...

71
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:13,793
wait.

72
00:03:14,043 --> 00:03:15,208
The wheel won't.

73
00:03:18,508 --> 00:03:19,176
Still.

74
00:03:19,176 --> 00:03:20,179
Go ahead.

75
00:03:20,179 --> 00:03:20,847
Build.

76
00:03:20,847 --> 00:03:22,184
Raise money.

77
00:03:22,184 --> 00:03:22,741
Ship.

78
00:03:23,041 --> 00:03:25,611
But your biggest asset isn't on that list.

79
00:03:25,961 --> 00:03:27,106
Your attention.

80
00:03:27,106 --> 00:03:31,685
We now stay on one screen about 47 seconds before switching.

81
00:03:31,685 --> 00:03:32,372
Guard it.

82
00:03:33,811 --> 00:03:34,547
Your mind.

83
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:40,438
In Anthropic's own trial, coders learning with AI scored 17 points lower on what

84
00:03:40,438 --> 00:03:41,911
they'd just learned.

85
00:03:41,911 --> 00:03:42,574
Train it.

86
00:03:43,938 --> 00:03:44,837
Your body.

87
00:03:44,837 --> 00:03:46,545
Your mental health.

88
00:03:46,545 --> 00:03:51,939
People who exercise report 43% fewer bad mental-health days.

89
00:03:51,939 --> 00:03:52,658
Move it.

90
00:03:54,175 --> 00:03:56,259
No release will update you.

91
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:57,263
Only you can.

92
00:03:58,263 --> 00:03:59,721
Invest consciously.

